{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/82875-momentum-embed","id":82875,"title":"Momentum Embed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-02T18:27:26-08:00","id":82875,"title":"Momentum Embed","content":"Just taking a poll on who would allow a demon to use Momentum on her first action of to fuel the second action she decides to take (essentially the demon would be treating herself as the secondary actor for her next roll). I ask because I can't really see anything specifically prohibiting it, especially seeing as the very first words of the embed write up are &quot;Any action&quot; and the only limitation placed at the end is &quot;The demon must see the target action take place and be in physical proximity and line of sight to the person taking the action&quot;, kinda hard to not be in physical proximity to ones self and not notice an action you're taking.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, opinions? Discuss!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T19:04:44-08:00","id":82893,"title":"","content":"The only thing I see specifically preventing it is that Momentum is basically a fancy teamwork action, which generally means you can't be a team by yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T20:45:09-08:00","id":82931,"title":"","content":"Haha, there is no &quot;I&quot; in team but there is a &quot;me&quot;. That\u2019s cool, so you'd go for the interpretation derived from the theme and example rather than mechanics then? I'm on the fence about either way as I understand exactly what you mean by the teamwork thing, but I also read the success part of the embed as &quot;The demon\u2019s player adds the successes of the preceding action to her next roll, <b>as if</b> the preceding were from a secondary actor using the Teamwork rules&quot;. For me &quot;as if&quot; makes it seem like the dice don\u2019t necessarily have to come from a secondary actor, just that they\u2019re treated as coming from someone else instead of just appearing in a pool. I\u2019m not too sure if giving extra dice from someones own roll would be any different than taking them from someone else. Really it just means the demon has to wait longer to get access to the extra dice and the only benefit I can think of is giving the player the ability to control if it\u2019s a dramatic failure. All in all, I\u2019d be happier if the embed just specifically stated if the target must be an external entity or not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T06:32:22-08:00","id":83137,"title":"","content":"Ah but there is an &quot;i&quot; in team. Its in the &quot;A&quot; hole! <br /> <br /> Joking aside, the embed does make it sound like there needs to be another person there. It seems heavily implied. The &quot;as if&quot; part seems to indicate that the preceding actor can be doing anything in the world, and yet still be treated as if he was being a secondary actor, normally a deliberate action. <br /> <br /> Given the fluff, it seems that the intent of the power is to be able to designate anyone doing anything as a secondary action, even if its an opponent. Designating yourself as a secondary actor really seems to stretch the intent of both teamwork rules, and of the power. It feels very rules-lawyer-y to me, twisting the spirit of the rule based on the definition of a pair of words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}